# The build context holds only what a Dockerfile COPYs; everything else (core_ws,
# the simulators, assets, weights) is bind-mounted at runtime, and sending it
# would cost about 11 GB per build. Deny all, then re-include the COPY sources:
#   unitree_sdk2_python                      BaseDockerfile, mac/BaseDockerfile.arm64
#   core_ws/src/livox_ros_driver2            RobocasaDockerfile, mac/RobocasaDockerfile.arm64,
#                                            mac/RosDockerfile.slim.arm64
#   core_ws/src/magpie_msgs                  IsaacDockerfile
#   docker/scripts/package_humble_runtime.py IsaacDockerfile
#   docker/locks/**                          every Dockerfile
#   docker/patches/**                        RobocasaDockerfile
# Their .git entries stay out.
*
!core_ws
core_ws/*
!core_ws/src
core_ws/src/*
!core_ws/src/livox_ros_driver2
core_ws/src/livox_ros_driver2/.git
!unitree_sdk2_python
!unitree_sdk2_python/**
unitree_sdk2_python/.git

!core_ws/src/magpie_msgs
core_ws/src/magpie_msgs/.git
!docker
docker/*
!docker/scripts
docker/scripts/*
!docker/scripts/package_humble_runtime.py
!docker/locks
!docker/locks/**
!docker/patches
!docker/patches/**
